course: dictionary
lesson: 96
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word «adder» is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context. «The adder, with a dark zigzag down its back, is Britain's only venomous snake.» The zigzag and the snake tell you that here adder means a snake.
explain: Now read this: «A part of the computer, called an adder, adds the numbers.» The word adds and the word numbers are the clues. Here an adder is a part of a computer that adds, not an animal. Always ask: which meaning fits the other words in the sentence?
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The adder bites only when stepped on or grabbed.» A snake that bites when stepped on makes sense. A computer part that bites does not. The swap check shows you the right meaning.
fact: Some words are spelled the same but have different meanings. This is called having more than one meaning.
fact: An adder is a small poisonous snake, and it is the only venomous snake native to Britain.
fact: The adder has a dark zig-zag pattern down its back, and another name for it is common European viper.
fact: An adder is also a part of a computer that adds numbers.
fact: The death adder is a different, very dangerous snake that lives in Australia.
exercise: «The adder, with a dark zigzag down its back, is Britain's only venomous snake.» What is an adder in this sentence? | A bird that sings at dawn | A kind of tall grass | *A small poisonous snake | A sum written on a board
exercise: «A part of the computer, called an adder, adds the numbers.» What is an adder in this sentence? | A type of bread | *A part of a computer that adds | A snake that hides in the heather | A mountain path
exercise: «The adder bites only when stepped on or grabbed.» What makes an adder bite? | Being sung to | *Being stepped on or grabbed | Being given milk to drink
test: «The adder is shy, and deaths from adder bites in Britain are very rare.» Which meaning of adder is used here? | *A small poisonous snake | A part of a computer that adds | A number that is added to another
test: Which country is the death adder from? | Ukraine | Britain | Scotland | *Australia
exam: Which meaning of adder fits a sentence about numbers? | A bite that needs a hospital visit | Another name for a common European viper | A snake with a zigzag back | *A part of a computer that adds
